<title>FRANCE: French crude imports, refining margins for July.</title>
<headline>French crude imports, refining margins for July.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's industry ministry on Thursday issued the following data for deliveries to refineries.</p>
<p>Crude deliveries are by origin ('000 tonnes). Total includes modest deliveries from domestic French crude production.</p>
<p>(Revisions for June 1996 are marked with an *)</p>
<p>					 July 1996  June 1996  July 1995</p>
<p>    Total				 8,095     *6,401	7,493</p>
<p>    including Saudi Arabia	  1,677     *1,242	2,260</p>
<p>		  Iraq			  0	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Iran		    1,044	  674	1,176</p>
<p>		  Kuwait		    271	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Algeria		    82	  320	  252</p>
<p>		  Libya		     249	   80	   80</p>
<p>		  Nigeria		 1,156	  561	  920</p>
<p>		  Britain		 1,001	  922	  740</p>
<p>		  Norway		  1,257	  967	1,075</p>
<p>		  ex-USSR		   811	  884	  377</p>
<p>The minstry also released the following data for French refining margins, based on North Sea Brent crude ($/barrel).</p>
<p>			    Aug 1996  Jul 1996  Jun 1996  Aug 1995</p>
<p>    Refining Margin     1.68	2.04	1.64	2.33</p>
<p>In the most recent month for which refinery capacity utilisation is available, French plants ran at 91 percent of capacity in July up from a revised 88 percent in June and down from 91 percent in July 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
